<title>MEXICO: Mexico sets tariff free egg import level for 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets tariff free egg import level for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Trade Ministry said on Thursday that 7,102.7 tonnes of egg could be imported in 1997 free of tariffs.</p>
<p>In a report in the Daily Gazette, the ministry said that most of the eggs exported from the United States are used in hotels and restaurants in Mexico-U.S. border towns. Other fertile eggs are used in laboratories and chicken farms.</p>
<p>The tariff-free imports are founded in the North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA) between Mexico, Canada and the United States.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
